    'body' => <<<'HTML'
<div class="key-takeaways"><h2>Key takeaways</h2><ul>
<li>A WPI-8 is the TDI windstorm certificate of compliance. Structures built or improved on or after Jan. 1, 1988 generally need one to be TWIA-eligible.</li>
<li>The WPI-1 is the application for that certificate. Starting April 1, 2026, WPI-1 applications must be certified to the 2024 IRC or 2024 IBC.</li>
<li>In the catastrophe area, re-roofs and roof repairs fall under the TDI windstorm inspection program, so most roof repairs after a claim need inspection.</li>
<li>The City of Corpus Christi requires a permit to re-roof, and the submission includes a completed WPI-1 form.</li>
<li>Code-driven costs are paid only if your policy has ordinance or law coverage, up to its limit.</li>
